 die and the  death urge was putting him in  circumstances trying to kill him to take  him to the realm of death or wherever it  is that he was supposed to go we know  this because over the course of the time  that they spent together death urge  would do things like have craig play  patty cake in the middle of the street  with oncoming traffic as like a toddler  or he would have them sit in a tree  during a lightning storm different  things along those lines right but what  ended up happening is there came a point  when death urge actually had craig  playing with matches in the basement of  his house and that it really would have  led to the death of pretty much anybody  under that circumstance and while it did  kill craig's father craig himself  survived and so craig's father was  whisked away by the death urge and then  craig himself was taken to a foster home  now one of those things that happened  there is the death urge kind of lingered  around there and it looked like one of  those circumstances where because craig  was just constantly abused by his father  that death urge was potentially  manipulating that we're not entirely  sure but during this time craig fell in  love with a girl named terry and the two  of them basically ended up going off  into the world and doing their own thing  but there came a point when terry just  couldn't handle it anymore because of  all the experiences she'd had over the  course of her life the abuse of the  hands of her father and so on and so  forth she had what seemed to basically  be ptsd left a suicide note for craig  and took her own life the belief of  craig is that the death urge goaded her  into doing it so craig basically told  death third i don't want to have  anything to do with you anymore go away  and effectively cast him off so any  belief that we had that death urge was  keeping craig safe from death was  immediately eliminated because following  the death of terry and the absence of  death urge that craig kept 